    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Cambodian empire founded in 802, whose god-kings ruled much of mainland <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a>.</li><li>Vast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reservoir">reservoirs</a> and canals fed a huge population and paid for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-wat">Angkor Wat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor-thom">Angkor Thom</a>, among the world's great monuments.</li><li>Strained waterworks, drought, Thai invasions and shifting trade led the court to abandon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angkor">Angkor</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phnom-penh">Phnom Penh</a> region.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>An inscription at the temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ta-prohm">Ta Prohm</a> records thousands of villages and attendants assigned to its upkeep, showing how temples worked as economic centres.</p></aside>
    </section>

